    "summary": "The finding was right: cleanup was gated on flags set after 'git worktree add' succeeded, but git can fail that command after it made the branch and directory (I confirmed with a failing post-checkout hook: exit 1 and both the worktree and the branch remain). executePark's finally now always runs, with no flags: 'git worktree remove --force <dir>', then remove the directory, then 'git worktree prune' (after the directory is gone), then 'git branch -D <tmp branch>'; each step is harmless when there is nothing to remove, so a half-made worktree is cleaned like any other. The second named test now installs a post-checkout hook that exits 1 in the parker's repo and parks: the result is 'park failed at making the temporary worktree', and assertClean shows only the main worktree in 'git worktree list', no 'insrc-park-tmp-*' branch, an empty temp directory, with the checkout snapshot (HEAD, branch, status, index, draft files) unchanged and the run still in the store; the hook is then removed and the rest of that test (failed note, second park on top, lost race, no remote) runs as before. Both named tests pass; team suite passes; tsc clean.",
